2026-02-10 11:33:52,814 - DocumentGraderNode - INFO: Retrieved document Similarly, the equity risk premium refers to the excess return that investing in the stock market provides over a risk-free rate. This excess return compensates investors for taking on the relatively higher risk of equity investing. The size of the premium varies and depends on the level of risk in a particular portfolio. It also changes over time as market risk fluctuates. is relevant
